work_units.notes:
In `benchbox/release/sync.py`, add:

  @dataclass
  class PublicRepoState:
      target_exists: bool
      target_clean: bool
      comparison: RepoComparison | None
      commits_ahead_of_last_tag: int
      commits_ahead_shas: list[str]   # "abbrev_sha - subject" lines
      last_tag: str | None

      @property
      def has_unexpected_divergence(self) -> bool:
          return self.commits_ahead_of_last_tag > 0 or (
              self.comparison is not None and self.comparison.has_conflicts
          )

  def check_public_repo_state(source: Path, target: Path) -> PublicRepoState:
      """Read-only programmatic equivalent of `benchbox-sync status`."""

Implementation reuses:
- `is_git_repo`, `is_repo_clean` (sync.py:38-51)
- `compare_repos` (workflow.py:1048)
- `git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match v*` for last_tag
- `git rev-list --count <last_tag>..HEAD` for commits_ahead_of_last_tag
- `git log --format='%h - %s' <last_tag>..HEAD` for commits_ahead_shas
Function MUST be read-only - no fetch, no commits, no mutations.
